course: dictionary
lesson: 11699
title: The word attire
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Attire is a grown-up word for clothes, especially the clothes you wear for a special event. Invitations often ask for it: «The invitation asked guests to wear formal attire.» The word formal tells you the clothes should be smart and grand, not everyday clothes.
explain: You can use the context to check. A party invitation, a school dress code or an old story often uses attire. In «The school dress code says smart attire is needed for the concert», the clues are school, concert and smart, so attire means the clothes you wear to look smart.
explain: Attire can also be a verb in old or formal writing. It means to dress someone. «The queen was attired in gold and silver» tells you she was dressed in gold and silver. Attired in is a common phrase, so when you see it, think dressed in.
fact: Attire means clothes, especially for a special event.
fact: «Formal attire» means smart, grand clothes for an important occasion.
fact: «Attired in» means dressed in, as in «attired in white».
fact: In everyday talk, people say clothes instead of attire.
fact: As a verb, attire is formal and old-fashioned: it means to dress someone.
exercise: «The invitation asked guests to wear formal attire.» What does attire mean here? | Empty rooms in a big house | A loud noise at night | A small animal with fur | *Clothes for a special event
exercise: «The king was attired in gold and silver.» What does attired mean? | Covered in mud | Tired | Hungry | *Dressed
exercise: Which everyday word means about the same as attire? | Weather | *Clothes | Shoes | Garden
test: «The school dress code says smart attire is needed for the concert.» What should Mia wear? | Her pyjamas | A swimming costume | A raincoat for the rain | *Smart clothes for the concert
test: Which phrase from the lessons means dressed in? | Formal sit | Dress code only | Smart walk | *Attired in
exam: Which phrase means clothes for a grand, special occasion? | Attire | Clothes for the garden | Attired by mud | *Formal attire
